Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): wait on busy near-cap accounts in drain pools
 (#6907)

Keep near-cap serialization and the quota recheck, but do not move a
busy account behind the remaining candidates solely because it is near
its cap when its pool is routed Until used up. Actual exhaustion still
hands the turn on. Other routing modes keep their spillover policy.

Carry the drain choice with each planned candidate so a nested group or
fallback retains its own routing instead of inheriting the outer request.
Following paul-tian's source analysis, this addresses drain semantics,
not the requested configurable policy for In order or new trace reasons.

Verification: TestDrainKeepsANearCapAccountThatIsBusy exercises the real
HTTP server with lanGuard, provider and group pools, nested drain groups
under order/pace/expiring, fallback providers, exhaustion and an order
control. The old outer-pool guard fails all nested and fallback cases:
sent map[acct-1:1 acct-2:1], want 2 on the first account. The fix passes.

